# env/ledger.env - the authorization ledger: one row per door (3.0). Plain in a private repository.
# ::STATE{@name, door:..., kind:..., ref:KEY | value:..., verify:<command, exit 0 = the door opens>, last_verified:YYYY-MM-DD|none, recover:<how to get back in>, scope:<tags>, top:true|false, why:<what it serves>}
# Values live here or in env/keys.env as KEY=value (ref:KEY). Top doors (root, payment, registrar, dns, account_security, recovery_code, age_identity) never unlock from the record; the owner issues a one-time code.
